sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-gasterosteus-doryssus-early-turing-wavelength-s0> a pk:Claim ;
        rdfs:label "Schnakenberg Turing wavelength of Gasterosteus doryssus_early at 33 µm (10.02 Ma) faithfully reproduces Gasterosteus doryssus_early morphology" ;
        dct:description "The simulation script(s) models/2026-delphi10000-gasterosteus-doryssus-early-turing-wavelength-s0.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Gasterosteus doryssus_early specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
        dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-gasterosteus-doryssus-early-turing-wavelength-s0.py> ;
        pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-gasterosteus-doryssus-early-turing-wavelength-s0.py; output: docs/media/gasterosteus_doryssus_early_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png; organism: Gasterosteus doryssus_early; environment: python 3.12.3, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.18.1, matplotlib 3.11.2, Pillow 13.0.0; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Turing (1952) dispersion relation and the critical wavenumber of a two-species reaction-diffusion system. | Schnakenberg (1979) kinetics du/dt = a - u + u^2 v, dv/dt = b - u^2 v. | Hunt, Bell & Travis (2008) and Bell, Travis & Blouw (2006): Truckee Formation G. doryssus pelvic reduction over about 22 kyr, with a complete pelvis at the start of the series (10.02 Ma in this slot's chronology). | Stuart, Travis & Bell (2020): Pitx1 contributes to pelvic reduction in this fossil lineage. | Nakamasu et al. (2009) and Kondo & Miura (2010): teleost chromatophores can sit in a Turing regime.; reconstructed_in_script: A 96² explicit-Euler Schnakenberg integration on a 280 µm patch, a 11-mode linearized dispersion test, a six-point D_u sweep, and an equal-diffusion ablation. | An m=2 spiral ocellus whose amplitude follows RMS(u), rendered as a 12-frame 640×480 GIF calibrated to the gallery photograph's orientation and radial spectrum.; transfer_boundary: The 32.86 µm length is the Delphi cellular-detail assignment. Bell, Hunt, and Stuart did not publish a pigment spacing. | Nakamasu/Kondo zebrafish chromatophore kinetics are not re-fit; a=0.062 and b=0.948 are a Jacobian that places the fastest mode at this wavelength. | The gallery image is a project species-gallery spiral with a 100 µm scale bar, not a Truckee thin section.; does_not_claim: That the fossil pelvis was measured at 33 µm, that the gallery band of 81.08 µm equals λ_c, or that doryssus_mid was integrated as a second PDE on this pass.]; phenomenon_size: 32 µm (3.168e-05 m, log10=-4.499 m, tier=4_cellular_10um); species_scale_ladder (10 runs from 32 µm to 9.9 cm): 32 µm:gasterosteus-aculeatus-bioelectric-polarity, 118 µm:gasterosteus-aculeatus-vertex-packing, 2.2 mm:gasterosteus-aculeatus-turing-wavelength, 4.1 mm:gasterosteus-aculeatus-clock-wavefront, 9.6 mm:gasterosteus-aculeatus-elastic-buckling, 1.3 cm:gasterosteus-aculeatus-morphogen-condensation, 1.7 cm:gasterosteus-aculeatus-flux-canalization, 2.2 cm:gasterosteus-aculeatus-branching-tree" ;
        pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1016/0022-5193(79)90042-0>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1038/s41559-020-01287-x>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.0808622106>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1098/rstb.1952.0012>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1558-5646.2007.00310.x>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1179047>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1666/05026.1> .
    <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-gasterosteus-doryssus-early-turing-wavelength-s0.py> a schema:SoftwareSourceCode ;
        rdfs:label "models/2026-delphi10000-gasterosteus-doryssus-early-turing-wavelength-s0.py" ;
        schema:codeRepository <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib> ;
        schema:programmingLanguage "Python" .
}

